      "audioScript": "What topic are you investigating for the unit on traffic, films, and festivals?\nI am presenting about Mid-Autumn Festival Lantern Parade and Mooncakes at village square.\nWhat is the most memorable aspect of this topic?\nAudiences and participants are amazed by star-shaped colourful lanterns and enjoy tasting baked mooncakes.\nHow does it teach students valuable lessons?\nIt promotes vibrant lion dances and emphasizes the vital role of drumming rhythms.\nThat is fascinating! The whole class will learn so much from your talk.",
      "clozeText": "Studying modern transportation, cinematography, and world celebrations enriches our global awareness. Whether located in village square or on international screens, this subject highlights the value of (23) ________. When traveling on roads or attending festivals, citizens (24) ________ obey safety guidelines strictly. Many young people find that tasting baked mooncakes provides memorable moments of (25) ________ and cultural learning. Although there are challenges in traffic management or film production, star-shaped colourful lanterns continues to (26) ________ millions of people. In conclusion, respecting rules and embracing diverse cultures will create a (27) ________ global community.",
      "readingText": "Mid-Autumn Festival Lantern Parade and Mooncakes offers a compelling perspective on contemporary society and cultural traditions in village square. Every year, thousands of people experience star-shaped colourful lanterns and celebrate vibrant lion dances, generating widespread public enthusiasm. Participants who engage in tasting baked mooncakes gain deeper insights into community solidarity and civic responsibility. Safety supervisors and creative artists emphasize drumming rhythms to ensure activities run smoothly without compromising public wellbeing. Furthermore, whether navigating bustling traffic corridors or immersing in cinematic masterpieces, learners develop critical thinking. By balancing modern technological progress with time-honoured cultural festivities, communities flourish with vitality and mutual respect.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nStudying modern transportation, cinematography, and world celebrations enriches our global awareness. Whether located in village square or on international screens, this subject highlights the value of (23) ________. When traveling on roads or attending festivals, citizens (24) ________ obey safety guidelines strictly. Many young people find that tasting baked mooncakes provides memorable moments of (25) ________ and cultural learning. Although there are challenges in traffic management or film production, star-shaped colourful lanterns continues to (26) ________ millions of people. In conclusion, respecting rules and embracing diverse cultures will create a (27) ________ global community.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nMid-Autumn Festival Lantern Parade and Mooncakes offers a compelling perspective on contemporary society and cultural traditions in village square. Every year, thousands of people experience star-shaped colourful lanterns and celebrate vibrant lion dances, generating widespread public enthusiasm. Participants who engage in tasting baked mooncakes gain deeper insights into community solidarity and civic responsibility. Safety supervisors and creative artists emphasize drumming rhythms to ensure activities run smoothly without compromising public wellbeing. Furthermore, whether navigating bustling traffic corridors or immersing in cinematic masterpieces, learners develop critical thinking. By balancing modern technological progress with time-honoured cultural festivities, communities flourish with vitality and mutual respect.",
