      "audioScript": "What topic are you investigating for the unit on traffic, films, and festivals?\nI am presenting about Zebra Crossings and Pavement Etiquette in Cities at pedestrian boulevard.\nWhat is the most memorable aspect of this topic?\nAudiences and participants are amazed by white painted zebra stripes and enjoy stopping for pedestrians.\nHow does it teach students valuable lessons?\nIt promotes clear obstacle-free sidewalks and emphasizes the vital role of city traffic planner.\nThat is fascinating! The whole class will learn so much from your talk.",
      "clozeText": "Studying modern transportation, cinematography, and world celebrations enriches our global awareness. Whether located in pedestrian boulevard or on international screens, this subject highlights the value of (23) ________. When traveling on roads or attending festivals, citizens (24) ________ obey safety guidelines strictly. Many young people find that stopping for pedestrians provides memorable moments of (25) ________ and cultural learning. Although there are challenges in traffic management or film production, white painted zebra stripes continues to (26) ________ millions of people. In conclusion, respecting rules and embracing diverse cultures will create a (27) ________ global community.",
      "readingText": "Zebra Crossings and Pavement Etiquette in Cities offers a compelling perspective on contemporary society and cultural traditions in pedestrian boulevard. Every year, thousands of people experience white painted zebra stripes and celebrate clear obstacle-free sidewalks, generating widespread public enthusiasm. Participants who engage in stopping for pedestrians gain deeper insights into community solidarity and civic responsibility. Safety supervisors and creative artists emphasize city traffic planner to ensure activities run smoothly without compromising public wellbeing. Furthermore, whether navigating bustling traffic corridors or immersing in cinematic masterpieces, learners develop critical thinking. By balancing modern technological progress with time-honoured cultural festivities, communities flourish with vitality and mutual respect.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nStudying modern transportation, cinematography, and world celebrations enriches our global awareness. Whether located in pedestrian boulevard or on international screens, this subject highlights the value of (23) ________. When traveling on roads or attending festivals, citizens (24) ________ obey safety guidelines strictly. Many young people find that stopping for pedestrians provides memorable moments of (25) ________ and cultural learning. Although there are challenges in traffic management or film production, white painted zebra stripes continues to (26) ________ millions of people. In conclusion, respecting rules and embracing diverse cultures will create a (27) ________ global community.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nZebra Crossings and Pavement Etiquette in Cities offers a compelling perspective on contemporary society and cultural traditions in pedestrian boulevard. Every year, thousands of people experience white painted zebra stripes and celebrate clear obstacle-free sidewalks, generating widespread public enthusiasm. Participants who engage in stopping for pedestrians gain deeper insights into community solidarity and civic responsibility. Safety supervisors and creative artists emphasize city traffic planner to ensure activities run smoothly without compromising public wellbeing. Furthermore, whether navigating bustling traffic corridors or immersing in cinematic masterpieces, learners develop critical thinking. By balancing modern technological progress with time-honoured cultural festivities, communities flourish with vitality and mutual respect.",
