      "audioScript": "What environmental, shopping, or disaster response issue are you reviewing?\nI am presenting about River Clean-Up Campaigns and Plastic Pollution in Can Tho at Hau River canals.\nWhat is the most critical aspect of this situation?\nExperts and citizens are paying close attention to floating plastic waste barriers and promoting removing river debris.\nHow does it safeguard human communities or foster sustainability?\nIt mitigates collecting discarded bags and emphasizes the vital function of volunteer green youth brigade.\nOutstanding! This presentation addresses urgent real-world challenges.",
      "clozeText": "Protecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In Hau River canals, stakeholders are addressing floating plastic waste barriers to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in removing river debris, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and volunteer green youth brigade guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "River Clean-Up Campaigns and Plastic Pollution in Can Tho addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing Hau River canals. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified floating plastic waste barriers, necessitating urgent action on collecting discarded bags. Citizens and volunteers who commit to removing river debris have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on volunteer green youth brigade to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nProtecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In Hau River canals, stakeholders are addressing floating plastic waste barriers to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in removing river debris, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and volunteer green youth brigade guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nRiver Clean-Up Campaigns and Plastic Pollution in Can Tho addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing Hau River canals. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified floating plastic waste barriers, necessitating urgent action on collecting discarded bags. Citizens and volunteers who commit to removing river debris have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on volunteer green youth brigade to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
