      "audioScript": "What environmental, shopping, or disaster response issue are you reviewing?\nI am presenting about Smart Shopping Strategies: Avoiding Impulse Consumer Purchases at supermarket aisle.\nWhat is the most critical aspect of this situation?\nExperts and citizens are paying close attention to pre-planned grocery lists and promoting refusing unnecessary discounts.\nHow does it safeguard human communities or foster sustainability?\nIt mitigates comparing unit prices and emphasizes the vital function of reusable shopping basket.\nOutstanding! This presentation addresses urgent real-world challenges.",
      "clozeText": "Protecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In supermarket aisle, stakeholders are addressing pre-planned grocery lists to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in refusing unnecessary discounts, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and reusable shopping basket guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Smart Shopping Strategies: Avoiding Impulse Consumer Purchases addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing supermarket aisle. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified pre-planned grocery lists, necessitating urgent action on comparing unit prices. Citizens and volunteers who commit to refusing unnecessary discounts have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on reusable shopping basket to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nProtecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In supermarket aisle, stakeholders are addressing pre-planned grocery lists to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in refusing unnecessary discounts, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and reusable shopping basket guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nSmart Shopping Strategies: Avoiding Impulse Consumer Purchases addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing supermarket aisle. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified pre-planned grocery lists, necessitating urgent action on comparing unit prices. Citizens and volunteers who commit to refusing unnecessary discounts have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on reusable shopping basket to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
