      "audioScript": "What environmental, shopping, or disaster response issue are you reviewing?\nI am presenting about Reducing Single-Use Water Bottles with Filtered Stations at school corridors.\nWhat is the most critical aspect of this situation?\nExperts and citizens are paying close attention to touchless water refilling fountains and promoting carrying reusable insulated flasks.\nHow does it safeguard human communities or foster sustainability?\nIt mitigates eliminating disposable plastic cups and emphasizes the vital function of environmental student club.\nOutstanding! This presentation addresses urgent real-world challenges.",
      "clozeText": "Protecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In school corridors, stakeholders are addressing touchless water refilling fountains to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in carrying reusable insulated flasks, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and environmental student club guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Reducing Single-Use Water Bottles with Filtered Stations addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing school corridors. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified touchless water refilling fountains, necessitating urgent action on eliminating disposable plastic cups. Citizens and volunteers who commit to carrying reusable insulated flasks have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on environmental student club to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nProtecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In school corridors, stakeholders are addressing touchless water refilling fountains to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in carrying reusable insulated flasks, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and environmental student club guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nReducing Single-Use Water Bottles with Filtered Stations addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing school corridors. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified touchless water refilling fountains, necessitating urgent action on eliminating disposable plastic cups. Citizens and volunteers who commit to carrying reusable insulated flasks have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on environmental student club to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
