      "audioScript": "What environmental, shopping, or disaster response issue are you reviewing?\nI am presenting about Traditional Village Bazaars and Fair Trade Produce at upland ethnic market.\nWhat is the most critical aspect of this situation?\nExperts and citizens are paying close attention to fresh mountain vegetables and promoting supporting local smallholder farmers.\nHow does it safeguard human communities or foster sustainability?\nIt mitigates honest bargaining etiquette and emphasizes the vital function of woven bamboo backpack.\nOutstanding! This presentation addresses urgent real-world challenges.",
      "clozeText": "Protecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In upland ethnic market, stakeholders are addressing fresh mountain vegetables to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in supporting local smallholder farmers, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and woven bamboo backpack guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Traditional Village Bazaars and Fair Trade Produce addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing upland ethnic market. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified fresh mountain vegetables, necessitating urgent action on honest bargaining etiquette. Citizens and volunteers who commit to supporting local smallholder farmers have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on woven bamboo backpack to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nProtecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In upland ethnic market, stakeholders are addressing fresh mountain vegetables to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in supporting local smallholder farmers, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and woven bamboo backpack guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nTraditional Village Bazaars and Fair Trade Produce addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing upland ethnic market. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified fresh mountain vegetables, necessitating urgent action on honest bargaining etiquette. Citizens and volunteers who commit to supporting local smallholder farmers have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on woven bamboo backpack to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
