      "audioScript": "What environmental, shopping, or disaster response issue are you reviewing?\nI am presenting about Urban Air Pollution and Low-Emission Green Zones at city center boulevard.\nWhat is the most critical aspect of this situation?\nExperts and citizens are paying close attention to real-time air quality monitors and promoting riding electric bicycles.\nHow does it safeguard human communities or foster sustainability?\nIt mitigates banning smoky diesel trucks and emphasizes the vital function of roadside tree green canopy.\nOutstanding! This presentation addresses urgent real-world challenges.",
      "clozeText": "Protecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In city center boulevard, stakeholders are addressing real-time air quality monitors to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in riding electric bicycles, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and roadside tree green canopy guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Urban Air Pollution and Low-Emission Green Zones addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing city center boulevard. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified real-time air quality monitors, necessitating urgent action on banning smoky diesel trucks. Citizens and volunteers who commit to riding electric bicycles have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on roadside tree green canopy to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nProtecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In city center boulevard, stakeholders are addressing real-time air quality monitors to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in riding electric bicycles, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and roadside tree green canopy guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nUrban Air Pollution and Low-Emission Green Zones addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing city center boulevard. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified real-time air quality monitors, necessitating urgent action on banning smoky diesel trucks. Citizens and volunteers who commit to riding electric bicycles have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on roadside tree green canopy to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
