      "clozeText": "Protecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In eco-friendly grocery shop, stakeholders are addressing gravity-fed dry food dispensers to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in weighing dried beans and grains, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and cotton produce pouch guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Zero-Waste Bulk Grocery Stores in Urban Quarters addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing eco-friendly grocery shop. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified gravity-fed dry food dispensers, necessitating urgent action on bringing glass refill jars. Citizens and volunteers who commit to weighing dried beans and grains have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on cotton produce pouch to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nProtecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In eco-friendly grocery shop, stakeholders are addressing gravity-fed dry food dispensers to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in weighing dried beans and grains, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and cotton produce pouch guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nZero-Waste Bulk Grocery Stores in Urban Quarters addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing eco-friendly grocery shop. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified gravity-fed dry food dispensers, necessitating urgent action on bringing glass refill jars. Citizens and volunteers who commit to weighing dried beans and grains have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on cotton produce pouch to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
