      "audioScript": "What environmental, shopping, or disaster response issue are you reviewing?\nI am presenting about Barcodes, QR Payments, and Cashless Supermarket Counters at hypermarket checkout.\nWhat is the most critical aspect of this situation?\nExperts and citizens are paying close attention to instant QR code scanners and promoting paying via smartphone wallet.\nHow does it safeguard human communities or foster sustainability?\nIt mitigates paperless digital receipts and emphasizes the vital function of self-service checkout kiosk.\nOutstanding! This presentation addresses urgent real-world challenges.",
      "clozeText": "Protecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In hypermarket checkout, stakeholders are addressing instant QR code scanners to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in paying via smartphone wallet, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and self-service checkout kiosk guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Barcodes, QR Payments, and Cashless Supermarket Counters addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing hypermarket checkout. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified instant QR code scanners, necessitating urgent action on paperless digital receipts. Citizens and volunteers who commit to paying via smartphone wallet have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on self-service checkout kiosk to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nProtecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In hypermarket checkout, stakeholders are addressing instant QR code scanners to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in paying via smartphone wallet, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and self-service checkout kiosk guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nBarcodes, QR Payments, and Cashless Supermarket Counters addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing hypermarket checkout. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified instant QR code scanners, necessitating urgent action on paperless digital receipts. Citizens and volunteers who commit to paying via smartphone wallet have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on self-service checkout kiosk to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
