      "audioScript": "What topic on gastronomy, tourism, or global linguistics are you presenting?\nI am presenting about Marine Ecotourism and Coral Reef Restoration in Phu Quoc at An Thoi archipelago.\nWhat is the most fascinating aspect of this subject?\nAudiences and experts are intrigued by transplanted nursery coral fragments and eager to practice snorkeling responsible dive sites.\nHow does it broaden our culinary knowledge or cultural horizons?\nIt showcases crystal clear turquoise shallows and highlights the significance of marine biology biologist.\nBrilliant! That will stimulate great discussions in our English classroom.",
      "clozeText": "Exploring international cuisines, eco-friendly tourism, and linguistic diversity enriches our teenage perspectives. In An Thoi archipelago, culinary masters and linguists emphasize transplanted nursery coral fragments as an essential element of cultural (23) ________. When travelers embrace snorkeling responsible dive sites, they promote environmental conservation and support local (24) ________. If someone wants to become a fluent international communicator, they (25) ________ master diverse dialects of English. Furthermore, understanding crystal clear turquoise shallows helps people appreciate foreign traditions without losing their own cultural (26) ________. In summary, respecting marine biology biologist paves the way for genuine global understanding and mutual (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Marine Ecotourism and Coral Reef Restoration in Phu Quoc represents an intriguing facet of modern globalization, culinary refinement, and cross-cultural exchange in An Thoi archipelago. Whether preparing delicate regional dishes or examining phonetic nuances, this subject combines transplanted nursery coral fragments with crystal clear turquoise shallows. Travelers and researchers who practice snorkeling responsible dive sites gain deep appreciation for the social customs that nurture human connection. Hospitality experts and educators highlight marine biology biologist as a benchmark for sustainable cultural preservation and ethical tourism. Moreover, mastering English as a global language equips Vietnamese teenagers to share our nation's wonders with foreign audiences. By harmonizing local gastronomy, ecological responsibility, and linguistic proficiency, students step confidently onto the global stage.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nExploring international cuisines, eco-friendly tourism, and linguistic diversity enriches our teenage perspectives. In An Thoi archipelago, culinary masters and linguists emphasize transplanted nursery coral fragments as an essential element of cultural (23) ________. When travelers embrace snorkeling responsible dive sites, they promote environmental conservation and support local (24) ________. If someone wants to become a fluent international communicator, they (25) ________ master diverse dialects of English. Furthermore, understanding crystal clear turquoise shallows helps people appreciate foreign traditions without losing their own cultural (26) ________. In summary, respecting marine biology biologist paves the way for genuine global understanding and mutual (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nMarine Ecotourism and Coral Reef Restoration in Phu Quoc represents an intriguing facet of modern globalization, culinary refinement, and cross-cultural exchange in An Thoi archipelago. Whether preparing delicate regional dishes or examining phonetic nuances, this subject combines transplanted nursery coral fragments with crystal clear turquoise shallows. Travelers and researchers who practice snorkeling responsible dive sites gain deep appreciation for the social customs that nurture human connection. Hospitality experts and educators highlight marine biology biologist as a benchmark for sustainable cultural preservation and ethical tourism. Moreover, mastering English as a global language equips Vietnamese teenagers to share our nation's wonders with foreign audiences. By harmonizing local gastronomy, ecological responsibility, and linguistic proficiency, students step confidently onto the global stage.",
