      "audioScript": "What topic on gastronomy, tourism, or global linguistics are you presenting?\nI am presenting about Australian English Slang and Indigenous Vocabulary at Sydney cultural center.\nWhat is the most fascinating aspect of this subject?\nAudiences and experts are intrigued by unique shortened slang terms and eager to practice analyzing colloquial Australian speech.\nHow does it broaden our culinary knowledge or cultural horizons?\nIt showcases aboriginal loanwords for wildlife and highlights the significance of Australian idiom guidebook.\nBrilliant! That will stimulate great discussions in our English classroom.",
      "clozeText": "Exploring international cuisines, eco-friendly tourism, and linguistic diversity enriches our teenage perspectives. In Sydney cultural center, culinary masters and linguists emphasize unique shortened slang terms as an essential element of cultural (23) ________. When travelers embrace analyzing colloquial Australian speech, they promote environmental conservation and support local (24) ________. If someone wants to become a fluent international communicator, they (25) ________ master diverse dialects of English. Furthermore, understanding aboriginal loanwords for wildlife helps people appreciate foreign traditions without losing their own cultural (26) ________. In summary, respecting Australian idiom guidebook paves the way for genuine global understanding and mutual (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Australian English Slang and Indigenous Vocabulary represents an intriguing facet of modern globalization, culinary refinement, and cross-cultural exchange in Sydney cultural center. Whether preparing delicate regional dishes or examining phonetic nuances, this subject combines unique shortened slang terms with aboriginal loanwords for wildlife. Travelers and researchers who practice analyzing colloquial Australian speech gain deep appreciation for the social customs that nurture human connection. Hospitality experts and educators highlight Australian idiom guidebook as a benchmark for sustainable cultural preservation and ethical tourism. Moreover, mastering English as a global language equips Vietnamese teenagers to share our nation's wonders with foreign audiences. By harmonizing local gastronomy, ecological responsibility, and linguistic proficiency, students step confidently onto the global stage.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nExploring international cuisines, eco-friendly tourism, and linguistic diversity enriches our teenage perspectives. In Sydney cultural center, culinary masters and linguists emphasize unique shortened slang terms as an essential element of cultural (23) ________. When travelers embrace analyzing colloquial Australian speech, they promote environmental conservation and support local (24) ________. If someone wants to become a fluent international communicator, they (25) ________ master diverse dialects of English. Furthermore, understanding aboriginal loanwords for wildlife helps people appreciate foreign traditions without losing their own cultural (26) ________. In summary, respecting Australian idiom guidebook paves the way for genuine global understanding and mutual (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nAustralian English Slang and Indigenous Vocabulary represents an intriguing facet of modern globalization, culinary refinement, and cross-cultural exchange in Sydney cultural center. Whether preparing delicate regional dishes or examining phonetic nuances, this subject combines unique shortened slang terms with aboriginal loanwords for wildlife. Travelers and researchers who practice analyzing colloquial Australian speech gain deep appreciation for the social customs that nurture human connection. Hospitality experts and educators highlight Australian idiom guidebook as a benchmark for sustainable cultural preservation and ethical tourism. Moreover, mastering English as a global language equips Vietnamese teenagers to share our nation's wonders with foreign audiences. By harmonizing local gastronomy, ecological responsibility, and linguistic proficiency, students step confidently onto the global stage.",
      "writingRubric": "Bố cục rõ ràng (0.25đ) - Ngữ pháp & Từ vựng chính xác (0.5đ) - Tính liên kết mạch lạc (0.25đ)",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my view, Australian English Slang and Indigenous Vocabulary represents a wonderful opportunity for cultural appreciation. Located in Sydney cultural center, it celebrates unique shortened slang terms and demonstrates how local heritage thrives. Taking part in analyzing colloquial Australian speech enriches our understanding of community values and promotes aboriginal loanwords for wildlife. Furthermore, respecting Australian idiom guidebook reinforces ethical tourism and international understanding. I look forward to exploring more of these rich cultural traditions.",
